description:
Found s504 by s501t (op/gmagic.t, left to s501t by Fable).  PRE-EXISTING (main b7ec0093 dies earlier: `tie $$s` with an undef $s was left untied; s501t fixed that half in p-cast-$-box -- gmagic 60/1 -> 61/3, the file still aborts at the same form).

Reproducer (perl prints `A 73 3 2 / B Tie::Monitor / C 73 3 2`):
    package Tie::Monitor;
    sub TIESCALAR { my($class, $value) = @_; bless [$value, 0, 0] }
    sub FETCH { ++$_[0][1]; $_[0][0] }
    sub STORE { ++$_[0][2]; $_[0][0] = $_[1] }
    sub init { my ($s) = @_; my @r = @$s[1,2]; @$s[1,2] = (0,0); "@r" }
    package main;
    my $s; tie $$s, "Tie::Monitor"; $$s = undef; $$s->[0] = 73;
    print "A ", $$s->[0], " ", (tied $$s)->init, "\n";
    my @a; tie $a[0], "Tie::Monitor"; print "B ", ref(tied $a[0]), "\n";
    $a[0] = undef; $a[0][0] = 73; print "C $a[0][0] ", (tied $a[0])->init, "\n";
PCL (s501t tree): `A  3 3` (the vivified array never reaches the tied scalar: the element write lands in a temporary; FETCH/STORE counts 3/3 vs 3/2), `B Tie::Monitor`, then `Can't call method "init" on an undefined value` -- `$a[0] = undef` (or the autoviv) REPLACES the tied element's box, so `tied $a[0]` is undef.
Family: the scalar-tie proxy (#1950, #1813); perl's rule: an rvalue-deref autoviv of a magical scalar FETCHes, builds the container, STOREs it, FETCHes it back (the same order s501t built for a tied AGGREGATE's element, %p-viv-result).  t/op/gmagic.t rows 90-121 + the five aborted forms are behind it.
